-----------------------------------------------------------------
                  Part 1:  Program Information:
-----------------------------------------------------------------

Program Name, Category, Keywords:
---------------------------------
   Name     - Mathweb
   Category - Psion3a (Math Assistant/Analysis Tool)
   Keywords - MATH
              ANALYSIS
              TOOL
              HYPERTEXT
              DATABASE
              CALCULATOR
              PROGRAMMING
              LANGUAGE
              PSION3A

Short Description:
------------------
Mathweb is a mathematical assistant, programming language, and
analysis tool. It computes using webs of arithmetic or string
expressions, builtin and user defined functions, and scripts of a
general purpose programming language.  For registered users, a
builtin x-y plotting feature can be activated, which automatically
generates plots of chosen pairs of variables during computation.

Medium Description:
-------------------
Mathweb is a mathematical assistant, programming language, and
analysis tool. It computes using webs of arithmetic or string
expressions, builtin and user defined functions, and scripts of a
general purpose programming language.  For registered users, a
builtin x-y plotting feature can be activated, which automatically
generates plots of chosen pairs of variables during computation.

Mathweb's simple, cellular organization also provides the ability
to edit, store, search, and report on the contents of hypertext
webs of text, as well as webs of functions and arithmetic
expressions. These features help the user in the analysis of
complex issues, relationships and subjects.  

Longer Descrtiption:
--------------------------
Mathweb is a mathematical assistant, programming language, and
analysis tool. It computes using webs of arithmetic or string
expressions, builtin and user defined functions, and scripts of a
general purpose programming language.  For registered users, a
builtin x-y plotting feature can be activated, which automatically
generates plots of chosen pairs of variables during computation.

Mathweb's simple, cellular organization also provides the ability
to edit, store, search, and report on the contents of hypertext
webs of text, as well as webs of functions and arithmetic
expressions. These features help the user in the analysis of
complex issues, relationships and subjects.  

When you pay the $33 Mathweb registration fee, you receive a diskette
containing the latest version of the program, a printed
user's manual, a key to enable normal file dialogs, disable registration
reminders, and some sample webs illustrating typical applications of
the program.

    Cave -- A tutorial example illustrating how to navigate the
         hypertext webs used by Mathweb.

    Piggy -- A tutorial example which computes the amount of cash
         in a piggy bank.

    Payment -- Compute the monthly payment necessary to pay off
         a loan at a specified interest rate.

    Pert -- Find the critical path and estimated time for a
         construction project.

    Quotes -- A compendium of quotes by famous and not so famous
         people.

    RKutta -- Compute the numerical solution to the differential
         equation for simple harmonic motion.

    Roots -- Compute the roots of a polynomial using Newton's
         method and the method of bisection.

    Trapzd -- Compute the integral, to a desired degree of accuracy,
         of an arbitrary function.

    Matrix, Matrix2, and Solve -- Solve simultaneous linear equations,
         compute reduced row echelon form of a matrix, and invert
         matrices, all with builtin functions.

    Stats -- Compute discriptive statistics and show distribution
         function for a collection of data values.  Generate
         random numbers from  normal, exponential, and uniform
         distributions.

    Ca -- Illustrates the development of limit cycles in cellular 
         automata.

    Hebb -- Illustrates Hebbian learning using a delta rule.

These examples only touch the surface of the volume of possible uses
of Mathweb.  It's uses are limited only by available processor power,
memory, and the imagination of the user.  From time to time,
additional examples are published on the web page
http://www.earthnet.net/~eieio/.

E-mail support for Mathweb is available at:

    71270.1441@compuserve.com
and
    eieio@boulder.earthnet.net

-----------------------------------------------------------------
                Part 2:  Distribution Requirements
-----------------------------------------------------------------
The demonstration version of Mathweb may be freely distributed,
with the following restrictions: permission must be received to
distribute Mathweb on retail racks, on CDROMs, or bundled
with any other product.

BBSs - please name the file Mathwb.xxx.

When distributing Mathweb the following files must be distributed
together.

    MATHWEB.APP
    README.TXT
    VENDOR.DOC
    FILE_ID.DIZ
    CAVE.WEB
    AMORT.WEB
    PAYMENT.WEB
    LOGISTIC.WEB
    PERT.WEB
    PIGGY.WEB
    QUOTES.WEB
    RKUTTA.WEB
    FILTER.WEB
    SOLVE.WEB
    HEBB.WEB
    MATRIX.WEB
    CA.WEB
    PLOT.WEB
    ROOTS.WEB
    
Disk Vendors, Shareware Distributors and BBS(s) may charge a nominal fee
for distribution of the program. The recipient of Mathweb must be informed,
in advance, that the fee paid to acquire Mathweb does not relieve the
recipient from registering his copy of Mathweb if he continues to use it.
